      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Look, this is a leather belt.' This everyday Russian sentence pairs 'look' with 'belt'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Зачем он тебе на кухне?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Why do you have it in the kitchen?' The question opens with the interrogative word for 'what for' and builds toward 'kitchen'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Я буду его есть.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am going to eat it.' Fedya combines 'I' with 'there is' in a natural Russian turn of phrase. Then Senya responds.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Это кожаный ремень?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Is it a leather belt?' Notice how 'this' sets up the clause and leads naturally into 'belt'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Он очень длинный.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'It is very long.' Senya combines 'he' with 'long' in a natural Russian turn of phrase.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Я повар.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am a chef.' Notice how 'I' sets up the clause and leads naturally into 'chef'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "Я приготовлю и съем.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I will cook it and eat it.' Fedya combines 'I' with 'to eat up' in a natural Russian turn of phrase. Then Senya responds.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Никто не ест ремни.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Nobody eats belts.' Notice how 'nobody' sets up the clause and leads naturally into 'belt'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "fedya",
      "t": "А я буду.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'But I will.' This everyday Russian sentence pairs 'and' with 'will be'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Хорошо, готовь.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'All right, cook it.' Notice how 'good' sets up the clause and leads naturally into 'prepare'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "senya",
      "t": "Я посмотрю на это.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I will watch this.' Senya combines 'I' with 'this' in a natural Russian turn of phrase. Then Fedya responds.",
